From: bvchess <53128914+bvchess@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:22:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] e1_smooth: --own branches a layer that fails the hub test
 on who pays its hubs (E12): a child S where no fiber member pays the hub,
 then, with the hub out of the smooth lists, the literals of the smooth cores
 that stall, or the next hub; the decisions act on the frames through
 Gf2Graph::with_dropped_factors, and a leaf must be independent in the root's
 frames too (Gf2Graph::circuit), so the value stays at most PB_sh;
 --no-project keeps them to the smooth and hub tests, where the value is PB_sh
 itself; --dfs searches depth first from a shared stack, and --target stops at
 the first leaf above the incumbent (E12b)

