+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Hub ownership (E12)
+//
+// A hub a (a smooth number) of layer k is listed by the fiber members a·q of layer k (q a prime above B) and by its
+// smooth members a·q (q ≤ B).  In a game either no fiber member pays with a (S), or one does and then no smooth member
+// does (F: each column pays one member).  A column that no member of a set pays with can be taken out of their lists
+// and the set stays playable, with the same order and payments.  So under S the game is playable in the instance where
+// the fiber members do not list a, and under F in the one where the smooth members do not.  In either its promotion set
+// is independent in every frame of that instance ([`Gf2Graph::with_dropped_factors`]: the frames with those factors
+// out of those movers' vectors), and it passes the smooth and hub tests with a taken from the fibers' hubs under S and
+// out of the smooth lists under F.  A node carries the hubs decided each way on its path (`own_s`, `own_f`); its bound
+// is the heaviest set of its instance, or its parent's bound where that is lower (a fixed row with a factor fewer can
+// free other elements, so the heaviest set of an instance can rise).
+//
+// At a layer that fails the hub test, the hubs its search turns on (`HubInfo`) are taken in order, as a chain.  For
